<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72001" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδ-αῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνόδιος</span>
			, of Hermes, Id. (s.v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδαῖα, τά,</span>
			<i>that for which a merchant travels, merchandise</i> (obtained in
			exchange for his <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρτος</span> or first
			freight), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.163
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.445
			</span></i> ; though a Sch. explains it as 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφόδια</span>
			, Lat. <i>viaticum</i> ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδάω.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>